Command Purpose Example <code>pwd</code> Print current directory <code>pwd</code> <code>ls -alh</code> List files with details <code>ls -alh</code> <code>cd</code> Change directory <code>cd training</code> <code>mkdir</code> Create directory <code>mkdir data</code> <code>touch</code> Create empty file <code>touch test.txt</code> <code>mv</code> Move/rename file <code>mv test.txt data.txt</code> <code>cp</code> Copy file <code>cp data.txt second.txt</code> <code>rm -rf</code> Remove file/directory <code>rm -rf extra/</code> <code>cat</code> Print file contents <code>cat data.txt</code> <code>grep</code> Search text patterns <code>grep "Unix" third.txt</code> <code>wc -l</code> Count lines <code>wc -l data.txt</code> <code>wget</code> Download file <code>wget URL</code> <code>zless</code> View compressed file <code>zless file.gz</code> <p>If you forget a command, use:</p> <pre><code>man &lt;command&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Example:</p> <pre><code>man cp
</code></pre>
